{"results":[{"entries":[{"dbId":"6803289","stId":"R-HSA-6803289","id":"R-HSA-6803289","name":"<span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span>","type":"Protein","exactType":"ReferenceGeneProduct","species":["Homo sapiens"],"referenceName":"<span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span>","referenceIdentifier":"P14174","compartmentNames":["ficolin-1-rich granule lumen"],"compartmentAccession":["1904813"],"isDisease":false,"hasReferenceEntity":true,"databaseName":"UniProt","referenceURL":"http://purl.uniprot.org/uniprot/P14174","disease":false},{"dbId":"212594","stId":"R-HSA-212594","id":"R-HSA-212594","name":"<span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span>","type":"Protein","exactType":"ReferenceGeneProduct","species":["Homo sapiens"],"referenceName":"<span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span>","referenceIdentifier":"P14174","compartmentNames":["extracellular region"],"compartmentAccession":["0005576"],"isDisease":false,"hasReferenceEntity":true,"databaseName":"UniProt","referenceURL":"http://purl.uniprot.org/uniprot/P14174","disease":false},{"dbId":"6803282","stId":"R-HSA-6803282","id":"R-HSA-6803282","name":"<span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span>","type":"Protein","exactType":"ReferenceGeneProduct","species":["Homo sapiens"],"referenceName":"<span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span>","referenceIdentifier":"P14174","compartmentNames":["secretory granule lumen"],"compartmentAccession":["0034774"],"isDisease":false,"hasReferenceEntity":true,"databaseName":"UniProt","referenceURL":"http://purl.uniprot.org/uniprot/P14174","disease":false},{"dbId":"8858256","stId":"R-HSA-8858256","id":"R-HSA-8858256","name":"AMH","type":"Protein","exactType":"ReferenceGeneProduct","species":["Homo sapiens"],"referenceName":"AMH","referenceIdentifier":"P03971","compartmentNames":["extracellular region"],"compartmentAccession":["0005576"],"isDisease":false,"hasReferenceEntity":true,"databaseName":"UniProt","referenceURL":"http://purl.uniprot.org/uniprot/P03971","disease":false}],"typeName":"Protein","entriesCount":4,"rowCount":4},{"entries":[{"dbId":"8950444","stId":"R-HSA-8950444","id":"R-HSA-8950444","name":"<span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> gene","type":"DNA Sequence","exactType":"ReferenceDNASequence","species":["Homo sapiens"],"referenceName":"<span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span>","referenceIdentifier":"ENSEMBL:ENSG00000240972","compartmentNames":["nucleoplasm"],"compartmentAccession":["0005654"],"isDisease":false,"hasReferenceEntity":true,"databaseName":"ENSEMBL","referenceURL":"https://www.ensembl.org/id/ENSG00000240972","disease":false},{"dbId":"8960626","stId":"R-HSA-8960626","id":"R-HSA-8960626","name":"AMH gene","type":"DNA Sequence","exactType":"ReferenceDNASequence","species":["Homo sapiens"],"referenceIdentifier":"ENSEMBL:ENSG00000104899","compartmentNames":["nucleoplasm"],"compartmentAccession":["0005654"],"isDisease":false,"hasReferenceEntity":true,"databaseName":"ENSEMBL","referenceURL":"https://www.ensembl.org/id/ENSG00000104899","disease":false}],"typeName":"DNA Sequence","entriesCount":2,"rowCount":2},{"entries":[{"dbId":"5676088","stId":"R-HSA-5676088","id":"R-HSA-5676088","name":"<span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> trimer","type":"Complex","exactType":"Complex","species":["Homo sapiens"],"compartmentNames":["extracellular region"],"compartmentAccession":["0005576"],"isDisease":false,"hasReferenceEntity":false,"disease":false},{"dbId":"5676093","stId":"R-HSA-5676093","id":"R-HSA-5676093","name":"<span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> trimer:CD74 trimer","type":"Complex","exactType":"Complex","species":["Homo sapiens"],"compartmentNames":["plasma membrane"],"compartmentAccession":["0005886"],"isDisease":false,"hasReferenceEntity":false,"disease":false}],"typeName":"Complex","entriesCount":2,"rowCount":2},{"entries":[{"dbId":"5676133","stId":"R-HSA-5676133","id":"R-HSA-5676133","name":"CD74 binds <span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span>","type":"Reaction","exactType":"binding","species":["Homo sapiens"],"summation":"Macrophage migration inhibitory factor (<span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span>), one of the first cytokines to be described (George & Vaughan 1962), is an important regulator of innate and adaptive immunity. <span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> is an upstream activator of monocytes/macrophages, centrally involved in the pathogenesis of septic shock, arthritis, and other inflammatory conditions (Nishihira 2000, Sanchez-Niño et al. 2013). High-expression <span class=\"highlighting\" >Mif</span> alleles are linked to severe rheumatoid arthritis (Morand & Leech 2005). <span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> promotes monocyte/macrophage activation and it is required for the optimal expression of TNF-alpha, IL-1, and PGE2 (Calandra & Bucala 1997). <span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span>-treated macrophages are more phagocytic and better able to destroy intracellular pathogens, such as Leishmania (Rosado & Rodriguez-Sosa 2011). Active <span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> is a 37.5 kDa homotrimer. <br><br><span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> can bind to CD74 (Leng et al. 2003) and the chemokine receptors CXCR2 and CXCR4 (Bernhagen et al. 2007). Leukocyte recruitment by <span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> is mediated by interaction with CXCR2 and CXCR4 (Bernhagen et al. 2007). <span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> interaction with CD74 mediates its proproliferative and antiproliferative effects, regulation of B-cell and tumor cell survival, fibrosis and angiogenesis (Starlets et al. 2006). <span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> can suppress the immunosuppressive effects of glucocorticoids, inducing a sustained pattern of ERK-1/2 MAP kinase activation (Bach et al. 2009). <br><br><span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> is endocytosed to bind the cytosolic protein JAB1 (Schwartz et al. 2012), negatively regulating JAB1-controlled pathways (Kleemann et al. 2000). <span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> inhibits JAB1-induced JNK activity, AP-1 activity and JAB1-dependent cell-cycle regulation by stabilizing p27Kip1 protein (Nguyen et al. 2003). Consequently, <span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span> blocks JAB1-mediated rescue of fibroblasts from growth arrest (Kleemann et al. 2000).","compartmentNames":["extracellular region","plasma membrane"],"compartmentAccession":["0005576","0005886"],"isDisease":false,"hasReferenceEntity":false,"disease":false},{"dbId":"8950732","stId":"R-HSA-8950732","id":"R-HSA-8950732","name":"Expression of Macrophage migration inhibitory factor","type":"Reaction","exactType":"omitted","species":["Homo sapiens"],"summation":"Experiments using human cord blood CD4(+) T cells show 22 protein spots and 20 protein spots, upregulated and downregulated proteins respectively, following Interleukin-12 stimulation (Rosengren et.al, 2005). Among the up-regulated proteins is :Macrophage migration inhibitory factor(<span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span>).","compartmentNames":["secretory granule lumen","nucleoplasm"],"compartmentAccession":["0034774","0005654"],"isDisease":false,"hasReferenceEntity":false,"disease":false}],"typeName":"Reaction","entriesCount":2,"rowCount":2},{"entries":[{"dbId":"A9UHW6-2","stId":"A9UHW6-2","id":"A9UHW6-2","name":"MIF4GD","type":"Interactor","exactType":"Interactor","species":["Homo sapiens"],"referenceIdentifier":"A9UHW6-2","databaseName":"UniProt","referenceURL":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/A9UHW6-2/entry"}],"typeName":"Interactor","entriesCount":1,"rowCount":1},{"entries":[{"dbId":"8950505","stId":"R-HSA-8950505","id":"R-HSA-8950505","name":"Gene and protein expression by JAK-STAT signaling after Interleukin-12 stimulation","type":"Pathway","exactType":"Pathway","species":["Homo sapiens"],"summation":"Experiments using human cord blood CD4(+) T cells show 22 protein spots and 20 protein spots, upregulated and downregulated proteins respectively, following Interleukin-12 stimulation (Rosengren et.al, 2005).\n The identified upregulated proteins are:  BOLA2, PSME2,  MTAP, CA1,  GSTA2,  RALA,  CNN2,  CFL1,  TCP1,  HNRNPDL,  <span class=\"highlighting\" >MIF</span>,  AIP,  SOD1, PPIA and  PDCD4.<br>And the identified downregulated proteins are:<br>ANXA2, RPLP0, CAPZA1, SOD2, SNRPA1, LMNB1, LCP1, HSPA9, SERPINB2, HNRNPF, TALDO1, PAK2, TCP1, HNRNPA2B1, MSN, PITPNA, ARF1, SOD2, ANXA2, CDC42, RAP1B and GSTO1.","compartmentNames":["nucleoplasm"],"compartmentAccession":["0005654"],"isDisease":false,"hasReferenceEntity":false,"hasEHLD":false,"disease":false}],"typeName":"Pathway","entriesCount":1,"rowCount":1}],"rowCount":12,"numberOfGroups":6,"numberOfMatches":12}